"</inlinemediaobject>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2385
msgid "The icon for a pie plot of the style with separated slices."
msgstr "Ikon för cirkeldiagram med åtskilda sektorer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2626
msgid "Ring Plots"
msgstr "Ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2630
msgid ""
"Ring plots present the numeric values of categorical data as segments of "
"circular rings. Sequential data values are considered to belong to different"
" categories and are plotted with distinct patterns. The data values from "
"different series are assigned to these categories based on the position of "
"the value in the series, for example, the second data value taken from each "
"series all share one category. The data values are used to determine the "
"size of the arc based on the proportionate size of the data value to the sum"
" of all data values in the series. For example, if the series had values { "
"1.12, 4.48, 3.36, 1.68, 0.56}, the contribution of each ring section to the "
"total would be {0.10, 0.40, 0.330, 0.15, 0.0 5}, since <literal>0.10= "
"1.12/(1.12+4.48+3.36+1.68+0.56)</literal>, and the angular arcs of the "
"sections would be {36, 144, 108, 54, 18} degrees, since "
"<literal>36=0.10*360</literal>."
msgstr ""
"Ringdiagram visar numeriska kategorivärden som segment i koncentriska "
"ringar. Värden i följd hör till olika kategorier och visas med olika "
"mönster. Värden från olika serier kopplas till kategorier utifrån sin "
"position i serien; det andra värdet i varje serie hör till exempel till "
"samma kategori. Segmentens vinkel bestäms av respektive värdes andel av "
"summan i serien. Om serien till exempel innehåller värdena { 1.12, 4.48, "
"3.36, 1.68, 0.56}, blir segmentens andelar av summan {0.10, 0.40, 0.330, "
"0.15, 0.0 5}, eftersom <literal>0.10= "
"1.12/(1.12+4.48+3.36+1.68+0.56)</literal>. Segmentens vinklar blir då {36, "
"144, 108, 54, 18} grader, eftersom <literal>36=0.10*360</literal>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2650
msgid "Ring plots do not have any sub-types."
msgstr "Ringdiagram har inga undertyper."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2654
msgid ""
"Ring plot styles provide two choices. Ring plots can be plotted with all "
"segments linked into a single overall ring, with different series plotted "
"immediately adjacent to one another in sequentially larger rings. "
"Alternatively, the segments of the outermost ring can be split and float a "
"certain distance away from the next ring."
msgstr ""
"Ringdiagram har två stilar. Alla segment kan bilda en sammanhängande ring, "
"där serierna visas i intilliggande ringar med ökande storlek. Alternativt "
"kan segmenten i den yttersta ringen delas upp och skiljas från nästa ring."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2666
msgid "An example of ring plots"
msgstr "Exempel på ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2674
msgid ""
"A screenshot of a worksheet area showing a data table and two ring plots "
"made with those data."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbild av ett kalkylblad med en datatabell och två ringdiagram som bygger"
" på värdena."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2681
msgid ""
"This screenshot shows a table of data and two ring plots. The data consist "
"of a single data series organized in a row and starting with the word "
"\"Widgets\". The data consist of three series organized by row and starting "
"with the words \"Widgets\", \"Gadgets\", and \"Lumpets\". Each of these "
"series has values in five categories. The two graphs illustrate the two sub-"
"types of ring plots, the left most plot without any gaps and the right most "
"plot having the outer plot with gaps."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar en datatabell och två ringdiagram. Data består av en enda "
"dataserie i en rad som börjar med ordet ”Widgets”. Data består av tre "
"radorienterade serier som börjar med etiketterna ”Widgets”, ”Gadgets” och "
"”Lumpets”. Varje serie innehåller värden för fem kategorier. Diagrammen "
"visar de två undertyperna: det vänstra saknar mellanrum och det högra har "
"mellanrum i den yttersta ringen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2699
msgid ""
"Each series in ring plots can include three main elements and two error "
"elements, although only the value element is necessary. The series can have "
"a 'Name' element, which is a single text entry used to identify the series, "
"must have a 'Values' element, which is a sequence of numeric values, and may"
" have a 'Label' element, which is a sequence of text entries used to "
"identify the categories. All of these elements can be defined as references "
"to a region of the worksheet, as literally defined entries, or as formula "
"expressions which result in the correct type. The 'Label' element is shared "
"by all of the series. The legend added to a ring plot identifies the "
"different series, by default using the entries of the 'Name' element of each"
" series. The two error elements include a list for errors in the positive "
"direction and one for errors in the negative direction."
msgstr ""
"Varje dataserie i ett ringdiagram kan innehålla tre huvudkomponenter och två"
" felkomponenter, men bara värdekomponenten är nödvändig. Serien kan ha "
"komponenten ”Namn”, ett textvärde som identifierar serien. Den måste ha "
"komponenten ”Värden”, en följd av numeriska värden, och kan även ha "
"komponenten ”Etikett”, en följd av textvärden som identifierar kategorierna."
" Komponenterna kan anges som referenser till ett cellområde i kalkylbladet, "
"som fasta värden eller som formeluttryck som ger rätt datatyp. Alla serier "
"delar på komponenten ”Etikett”. Förklaringen i ringdiagrammet identifierar "
"serierna och använder som standard värdena i respektive series komponent "
"”Namn”. De två felkomponenterna innehåller listor med positiva respektive "
"negativa felvärden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2717
msgid "The data in each ring plot series"
msgstr "Data i varje serie i ett ringdiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:2765
msgid "Ring plots provide two icons distinguishing the two different styles."
msgstr "Två ikoner skiljer stilarna för ringdiagram åt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
